WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.2 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Working out which policies you actually need

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Choose policies from what you do and the harm it could cause.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Assess form, activities, geography, size, funders and risks.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Sort policies: needed now, needed soon, good practice.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Give each an owner, approver and review date.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Tide Line Youth Collective (Community group · idea stage, Indonesia)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Tide Line: safeguarding, adult conduct, consent and water safety now; finance after registration; HR only with the first paid role.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a prioritised policy register.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
